# Branch flow

Feature and fix work lands on `master` only after it has been merged to `devel` and verified there.

## Branches

- `master` — release branch. Do not commit feature work here.
- `devel` — integration branch. Verify here before release.
- One branch per issue, cut from up-to-date `devel`.

Name the issue branch `issue/<id>-<short-slug>` when an issue id exists. Otherwise use a short topic name with the same base and PR target (`fix/paging-search`).

## Flow

1. Update `devel`, then create the issue branch from it.
2. Commit the change on that branch only.
3. Open a pull request into `devel`. Do not open the feature PR against `master`.
4. Merge into `devel` only after review. Verify on `devel` (CI, and the checks the change needs) before any release PR.
5. Open a pull request from `devel` into `master`. Merge `master` only after that verification.

```text
issue/42-trend-field  →  PR  →  devel  →  verify  →  PR  →  master
```

## Do not

- Commit or push feature work directly on `devel` or `master`.
- Merge an issue branch straight into `master`.
- Open or merge the `devel` → `master` PR before `devel` verification has finished.
- Force-push `master` or `devel`.
